{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"prosaic-visionary-basilisk","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter the sibling story \"validity-only by default; no code path reads the repo-pinned trust file\" lands, no verification, signing, health or merge-gate path reads `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`. The file itself, its loader `src/rebar/attest/trusted_env.py`, and the `rebar trusted-env` command (`src/rebar/_commands/trusted_env_cmd.py`, parser factory `build_trusted_env` in `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/certs.py`, registry rows at `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py` lines 304 and 326, help `src/rebar/_cli/help/trusted-env.txt`) still exist. ADR 0125 removes them so no op-cert keys are pinned in the repository. Sequencing: built on the validity-only story's merged commit.\n\n## Approach\n1. Delete `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, `src/rebar/attest/trusted_env.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/trusted_env_cmd.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/trusted-env.txt`, and `tests/unit/test_trusted_env.py`.\n2. Remove `build_trusted_env` from `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/certs.py` (keep the `remote-cert` factory and update the module docstring), the two `trusted-env` rows from `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`, the `trusted-env` line from `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt`, and the `.gitignore` lines that un-ignore and describe the pin file (lines 21-28); a rule there that still applies to another file stays, with its comment reworded without the pin file.\n3. Drop `trusted-env` from the CLI test tables in `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py` and `tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6.py`; remove the pin-file test `test_trusted_env_pins_deployed_environment_log_position_form` (line 293) from `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py`, and replace the pin-file fixture in `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` (lines 444-553) with the trust-list form where the test still needs trust.\n4. Regenerate `docs/cli-reference.md` and any generated census the deletion changes (each failing drift test names its generator script), and run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` if the ratchet reports removed mechanisms as stale, committing the shrunk baseline that command writes.\n5. Update code docstrings that still name the pin file: `src/rebar/attest/opcert.py` (line 13) and `src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py`.\n\n## Scope\n- Deleted: `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, `src/rebar/attest/trusted_env.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/trusted_env_cmd.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/trusted-env.txt`, `tests/unit/test_trusted_env.py`\n- Edited: `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/certs.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt`, `.gitignore`, `src/rebar/attest/opcert.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py`, `docs/cli-reference.md`, `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (only via `--update-stale`)\n- Tests: `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py`, `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py`\nOut of scope: prose docs and runbooks (docs sibling); historical ADRs 0049, 0098, 0100, 0104 keep their text as records; eval corpora and fixtures under `evals/` and `tests/fixtures/` that quote the filename as data.\n\n## Testing\nRemoval only; the behaviour change already landed. The registry-cutover table asserts `rebar trusted-env` is no longer a registered command, the CLI help artifacts regenerate without it, and `make verify` passes. Portability: deletions only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, `src/rebar/attest/trusted_env.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/trusted_env_cmd.py` and `src/rebar/_cli/help/trusted-env.txt` do not exist on main (checked: `git ls-files` prints nothing for each path).\n- [ ] No code reads a repo-pinned op-cert trust file: `git grep -nF trusted_environments -- src` and `git grep -nF trusted_env -- src` print no hits.\n- [ ] `rebar trusted-env` is not a registered command (checked: `pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6.py -q`).\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `make verify` is green, and the change lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","id":"8145-b4c2-29f8-4012","parent_id":"0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Remove .rebar/trusted_environments.yaml, attest/trusted_env.py and the rebar trusted-env command"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795112644093565591,"uuid":"039c7302-5064-4193-a82d-b19ee1cd3ea5"}